{{GameData.player_name}}: Nothing could be better than this

Felix sits on the table beside you, staring at your breakfast as if he hasn't eaten in days

Despite his dramatic expression, he finished his own meal only a few minutes ago

After breakfast, you finish getting ready and head to the university

do SceneController.stop_video()
do SceneController.change_background("res://Visual Novel Romance/files/img2.png")

When you arrive, you meet your friend from the History department.

do SceneController.show_character("Sprite1")

Gio: Hey, {{GameData.player_name}}. Do you remember my last study about local folklore? I found more information about the stories we used to hear when we were children

You begin to remember the tales about dreams, where an Oneiric being protects the dreams of children and the world itself, keeping balance between them

The legend says that when people stop dreaming, the Oneirics lose their strength, leaving humanity vulnerable to the attacks of their greatest nightmares

Gio: Well, according to the book I'm reading, these stories are ancient and connected to rituals and ancestral temples

Gio: This book suggests that, if those practices truly worked, people could reach a state where they were able to control their dreams. Dreams could even become a way to understand the present or glimpse the future

Gio: I'm going to use this book for my research project. What did you think about it?

- Ask more about it
  => about

- Remember the childhood tales
  => tales

~ about
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("about")

{{GameData.player_name}}: That's incredible. Is this book from the university? I'd love to hear more about your research

Gio: Actually, I borrowed it from a small chapel not far from here. There are plenty of academic books on the subject, but I wanted firsthand accounts from people who actually lived through those experiences

Gio: That's what makes this one so fascinating. It was written by a monk who documented his entire journey, from his first encounters with those practices to the day he became a monk himself

The two of you continue talking until it's time for class

Once inside the classroom, you struggle to stay awake. After managing to copy a few notes, the lecture finally comes to an end

As everyone begins to leave, Gio catches up with you

Gio: Heading home? Want to walk together?

You nod, and the two of you leave the university side by side

=> work

~ tales
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("tales")

{{GameData.player_name}}: So... the stories our parents used to tell us actually came from this folklore?

{{GameData.player_name}}: There were so many of them, but I can barely remember any now

Gio: That's right. Over time, most people simply forgot them. Even so, many older generations still hold on to those legends

Gio: We even have festivals and traditions that keep the stories alive, though they're nothing like they used to be

{{GameData.player_name}}: I loved listening to those stories when I was a kid. But eventually everyone stopped talking about them

{{GameData.player_name}}: I remember attending ceremonies where people encouraged us to treasure our dreams and never give up on them

Gio: That's one of the core beliefs behind these traditions

Gio: Dreams are said to reveal who we truly are... or, sometimes, the parts of ourselves we're trying to hide

Gio: To stop dreaming, or to stop pursuing your goals, is like turning your back on your own identity

{{GameData.player_name}}: That's... actually a really interesting way of looking at it

{{GameData.player_name}}: I'd better get going. My class has probably already started

Gio: See you around.
do SceneController.hide_character("Sprite1")

