Beast: The rules are simple. Before us lies a deck of thirty-two cards. Each card bears the symbol of a chess piece. Every piece has its own value

Beast: Pawns are worth 10 points. Knights and Bishops are worth 30. Rooks are worth 50. Queens are worth 70

Beast: Kings do not deal damage. Instead, they restore up to 50 health

Beast: We each begin with the same amount of health

Beast: Three rounds. If your health reaches zero... your dreams become mine

Beast: If mine reaches zero... I'll return your precious cat. Should we both survive, victory belongs to whoever has the most health remaining

Beast: Shall we begin?

