~ not_tell
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("not_tell")
do SceneController.show_character("Sprite1")
{{GameData.player_name}}: I just had a terrible night... My cat ran away, and I still haven't found him

Gio: Oh... That's sad. You'll find him soon, I'm sure of it

Gio: So, how did this happen?

{{GameData.player_name}}: To tell you the truth, I don't even know... I was opening the door to get inside my house when my key fell to the floor, and during that time Felix, who was near the door, ran outside

Gio: I hope he's okay

{{GameData.player_name}}: Me too

{{GameData.player_name}}: Let's change the subject for a bit... Give my mind a chance to relax

{{GameData.player_name}}: You said you had discovered something new. What was it?

Gio: I can tell you're interested in my research

Gio: Well... There are several curiosities and mysteries surrounding these mystical beings

Gio: Nightmares are frequently associated with large animals, creating a sense of helplessness and terror, neutralizing their targets without much effort

Gio: Meanwhile, dream beings are often represented as small, bright, flying creatures

Gio: But it's funny how humans are sometimes represented as both, to suggest that deep down, we are the evil we fear and the good we desire

Gio: Stories always try to convey the idea that you should prioritize who you are over the person others expect you to be

Gio: The complete opposite of nightmares, which try at all costs to make you lose yourself

Gio: Dreams reveal a great deal about who you are, including what you think and feel

{{GameData.player_name}}: Hmmm... So what would it mean to dream about guardians and beasts?

Gio: I'm not an expert in the field... but I would assume it indicates some kind of conflict. I'm not certain, though. It depends a lot on what the dream was like

{{GameData.player_name}}: Ah... I see. That's really interesting, but I think it's time for class to start

Gio: True. See you later

You say goodbye and go to your respective classrooms. You wonder if you should have told him, but you're afraid of what it might trigger

You try to remember the church's commandments, hoping to find something that might help you, but you can't remember much

You wonder if you should talk to Ello to figure out how to deal with this

You struggle to focus on the class material because you don't want to fail the subject, so you take notes and draw to help with your thought process

After class, you head straight to work. On the way, you run into Mary

Mary asks how you are doing, and you briefly explain the situation. She sympathizes with you and says she'll give you a cat collar with a tracker to save you the trouble

Mary tells you about the latest news from her job and how well she's been doing at university this semester, although she still doesn't have much time to have fun

